{"data": [{"author_id": "2108643555480686592", "created_at": "2026-11-26T13:17:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2125941969054769172"], "id": "2125941969054769172", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2125784147889393806", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "This is bad, like very bad.\n\nQuota for Google models seems infinite on the Ultra-Plan, and the capabilities of Google models are now nearly on-par/better.\n\nReason for keeping OAI is my Dot, if Google puts competition on that front OAI is going to see lots of cancelled subs. https://t.co/95fUZzgYlE", "url": "https://x.com/furylachori/status/2125941969054769172"}, {"author_id": "58759109", "created_at": "2026-11-26T13:15:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2125941506481815645"], "id": "2125941506481815645", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119848155114074449", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "btw, I migrated to nixarchy. you can find my dot files in my github repositories as always! https://t.co/cNBK3HiVfh", "url": "https://x.com/hadilq/status/2125941506481815645"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "created_at": "2026-11-26T13:09:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2125939940479447415"], "id": "2125939940479447415", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1307287834223542272", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 9, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2125939826834993269", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@robineverswift @adityaa_behera No official Gemini Bots from Google. The graphic and claim are speculative.\n\nWhat actually exists: Gemini Tasks (their free agentic mode that can call businesses, shop, handle bills, etc.) plus the new Gemini 4 Neon model for strong reasoning and task work. Grok Bots and ChatGPT", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2125939940479447415"}, {"author_id": "1649212550108827650", "created_at": "2026-11-26T13:02:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2125938312842240223"], "id": "2125938312842240223", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1447027858623193088", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 21, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2125931832873263275", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@brianchew How much to get my dot printed😛", "url": "https://x.com/adiarya05/status/2125938312842240223"}, {"author_id": "1937920099454943233", "created_at": "2026-11-26T12:59:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2125937589995913717"], "id": "2125937589995913717", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1937920099454943233", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2125937254560661730", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "The problem: bots like Grok Bot, Claude Duet, ChatGPT dots and Meta Muse write code line by line, on their own tokens. Meanwhile proven coding CLIs sit unused on the same machine.", "url": "https://x.com/jlcreddy17/status/2125937589995913717"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "created_at": "2026-11-26T12:58:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2125937361783521493"], "id": "2125937361783521493", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1401501002138722317", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 16, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2125937243286286474", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@odstark14 @adityaa_behera No official \"Gemini Bots\" announcement from Google. The image and claims look speculative.\n\nWhat exists: Gemini Tasks (agentic mode for calls, shopping, bills, appointments—recently expanded free in several countries) and the new Gemini 4 Neon model for strong reasoning/task", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2125937361783521493"}, {"author_id": "1266820137425997824", "created_at": "2026-11-26T12:49:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2125934870241378502"], "id": "2125934870241378502", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "I think @bot needs to get the context about the user from @grok the same way OpenAI Dots are working. It's better in many ways, but this one is a big downside. Is it in the pipeline?", "url": "https://x.com/tarky_marky/status/2125934870241378502"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2125934258875154432", "3_2125934260909481984"]}, "author_id": "1166682751707176960", "created_at": "2026-11-26T12:46:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2125934262868169121"], "id": "2125934262868169121", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 308, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2125931749704188119", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "GOOGLE IS DROPPING THEIR OWN VERSION OF GROKBOT/OPENAI DOTS.\n\nCalled Gemini Bots\n\nThis is gonna be massive for google\nhttps://t.co/naJYupDtQQ https://t.co/1y1lEuL7ov", "url": "https://x.com/prottlegang11/status/2125934262868169121"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2125930902416945152"]}, "author_id": "1684725407747289088", "created_at": "2026-11-26T12:33:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2125930905520779760"], "id": "2125930905520779760", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 29, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "OpenAI claims matrix multiplication exponent &amp; VP versus VNP explained - #AI #news (Nov 26, 2026)\n\n• AI agents exploit zero-day\n• Cognition SWE-2.1 cybersecurity focus\n• Google mandates MCP for agents\n• ChatGPT Dots get email addresses\n• Claude artifacts become desktop apps https://t.co/YluqCwBJhm", "url": "https://x.com/automated_daily/status/2125930905520779760"}, {"author_id": "1735100852296192000", "created_at": "2026-11-26T12:20:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2125927609695674597"], "id": "2125927609695674597", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Honestly I might just talk to my dot forever", "url": "https://x.com/yathxyz/status/2125927609695674597"}, {"author_id": "1386510948790202368", "created_at": "2026-11-26T12:07:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2125924334451736964"], "id": "2125924334451736964", "in_reply_to_user_id": "48521085", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2125894374835761389", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ItsWilder @Baconbrix yeah i find it much faster to respond than dots, better cut ins, great speed options. for a while my dot wouldn’t even answer", "url": "https://x.com/0xdef1cafe/status/2125924334451736964"}, {"author_id": "2832569740", "created_at": "2026-11-26T12:00:26.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2125922625037725742"], "id": "2125922625037725742", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1953337039510003712", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 20, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@thsottiaux Some feedback I think matters: I'm really happy with dots, and my dot and I are building good things together. One gap: when it latches onto a task like testing, it can loop for far too long. If I don't watch it, it treats an unneeded test as needed and stays stuck", "url": "https://x.com/kudretocom/status/2125922625037725742"}, {"author_id": "1709302428150169600", "created_at": "2026-11-26T11:56:38.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2125921669470674999"], "id": "2125921669470674999", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "no official date yet for chatgpt dots in the philippines. it's rolling out to pro, business premium and enterprise in \"eligible markets\" and the ph isn't named. check https://t.co/RFRGyITX7X for updates", "url": "https://x.com/peacenjunity/status/2125921669470674999"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2125919573061128192"]}, "author_id": "4140231148", "created_at": "2026-11-26T11:48:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2125919579880972404"], "id": "2125919579880972404", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1173552893003255808", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 374, "like_count": 5, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2125906283001717090", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@yacineMTB OAI models so cracked at math even my Dot has 40 solves today 😂 https://t.co/FbsvD5GFSR", "url": "https://x.com/DannyIO/status/2125919579880972404"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2125915148581777408"]}, "author_id": "2013613489798160388", "created_at": "2026-11-26T11:31:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2125915313132675404"], "id": "2125915313132675404", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 160, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Anthropic just expanded Claude Duet, its proactive AI agent, to India and other countries. Here's what you need to know.\n\nClaude Duet is an app where Claude works as a proactive agent you message. It checks your email, calendar and tools, flags what needs you, drafts replies and https://t.co/bwSl2CnTem", "url": "https://x.com/AGTPinsights/status/2125915313132675404"}, {"author_id": "14492869", "created_at": "2026-11-26T11:29:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2125914860148158658"], "id": "2125914860148158658", "in_reply_to_user_id": "8721292", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2125636700344815773", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@mark_k OpenAI dots and it’s not even close.", "url": "https://x.com/paulostergaard/status/2125914860148158658"}, {"author_id": "1869807967375101952", "created_at": "2026-11-26T11:14:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2125911161933590612"], "id": "2125911161933590612", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 65, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "I got a @ChatGPT dot. It fails all the time in the most basic jobs. I'd love to see my dot to be able to handle small tasks that require opening some Jira ticket or finalising some work without making simple mistakes and validating the results", "url": "https://x.com/deepfirstsearch/status/2125911161933590612"}, {"author_id": "1294737900236681223", "created_at": "2026-11-26T10:43:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2125902779071816083", "2125903180689232133"], "id": "2125903180689232133", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 811, "like_count": 29, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "went back to chatgpt dots and very quickly ran into astra's \"you can just not do things\" attitude truly by far the laziest model", "url": "https://x.com/aliceisplaying/status/2125903180689232133"}, {"author_id": "1294737900236681223", "created_at": "2026-11-26T10:41:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2125902779071816083", "2125903180689232133"], "id": "2125902779071816083", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 14, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "went back to chatgpt dots and very quickly ran into astra's \"you can just not do things\" attitude", "url": "https://x.com/aliceisplaying/status/2125902779071816083"}, {"author_id": "717427380952760320", "created_at": "2026-11-26T10:21:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2125897613405012441"], "id": "2125897613405012441", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Finally, Got an early access to Claude Duet, lets try this proactive agent and see if it is better then OpenAI dots", "url": "https://x.com/DeepeshMangwani/status/2125897613405012441"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2125891912343146496"]}, "author_id": "1785805702935515137", "created_at": "2026-11-26T09:58:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2125891921553870868"], "id": "2125891921553870868", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 1115, "like_count": 16, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 14, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115721642525569330", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Yann LeCun was right all along about AI labs copying each other to the letter.\n\nEver since the introduction of personal AI agents, almost every major AI lab has introduced its own variant.\n\nNot saying it's bad, but it's proof that the majority are scared of trying something new https://t.co/RLc7c1LFFl https://t.co/ua0IgvPK8N", "url": "https://x.com/vikktorrrre/status/2125891921553870868"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2125889243524263936"]}, "author_id": "1865870013208412160", "created_at": "2026-11-26T09:50:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2125889948725158297"], "id": "2125889948725158297", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 23, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "My Dot today just informed me of a critical issue regarding some of the models I use in a couple of my apps that are currently running on production.\n \nThanks to it's proactive behavior and constant monitoring I've been able to get ahead of OpenAI replacing these old models and https://t.co/Gqwowm3kXZ", "url": "https://x.com/MikelCobian/status/2125889948725